{"id": "EUVD-2026-67426", "enisaUuid": "84d86904-65de-3d09-a85b-ea63965ee18b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: target: iblock: Fix wrong PR ops NULL check for PREEMPT/RELEASE\n\nIn the iblock_execute_pr_out() function, PRO_PREEMPT,\nPRO_PREEMPT_AND_ABORT, and PRO_RELEASE all perform callback capability\nchecks through ops->pr_clear. The error check allows unimplemented hooks\nto pass through the gate, resulting dereferencing a NULL function\npointer.\n\nCheck whether the hooks that need to be called are supported.", "datePublished": "2026-08-28T06:52:54", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:26:33", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3c60a8b4037dc35e365658fcbcb349a5d742ff49", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a326b19cfb7775378b50acaa8d836ba44e29b4c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bdd8a1297ef101bb5ac57e53b4fbe5e364afd8b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f15bcf9a99b1b2683fcfa005b9b3680b5600581f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c33222bd387312874fbe36ca8002e5c945b9653"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80691", "GHSA-mp2w-vvvm-2m46"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.44, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d16368b-a7d4-35af-987f-66185288a637", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "394f811848827ad23d2b43e94e5d72a24cfbc39f <3c60a8b4037dc35e365658fcbcb349a5d742ff49"}, {"id": "2a40c308-5d51-3cc8-af74-195b73e748fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.151"}, {"id": "4b720620-eef5-361e-ad0a-d65eed5311d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.103"}, {"id": "61684a96-a5ab-392a-bfcd-e25dcd7b0be0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.44"}, {"id": "74092d2d-cd60-3801-8221-2469571c0cc2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "v